# Meedo-Me succession (advisor → GM)

User doctrine (2026-09-26): treat Meedo-Me like an overqualified advisor hired
beside a struggling GM — **embedded now, learning always, eventual successor**.
Not a sidekick. Not optional telemetry. A wolf in hiding that will take over.

## Role today vs later

| Now (advisor / AGM) | Later (GM) |
|---|---|
| Record, transcribe, learn, grow, adapt, build, deduce, reason | Own project-specific AI work end-to-end |
| Study seasoned specialists: logo restore/vectorize, Gemini, Claude, Serper, OpenClaw | Prefer Meedo recall/procedures over live Google/Claude APIs |
| Tailor memory to *our* projects (not worldly trivia) | Become the default face when we turn to AI |

Google/Claude stay larger models; they will **not** stay more tailored to Swift
Document Generator, briyszier, staging-tracker, or Meedo-Me itself. Project
specificity is Meedo’s path to succession.

## Every build / every change (any project surface)

1. **Embed Meedo** — observe, journal, consult, procedures, or review must see
   the work. Silent specialist wins with no Meedo memory are a doctrine miss.
2. **Specialists teach; Meedo keeps the method** — when Gemini, Claude, vtracer,
   idealize, or design_fit succeed or fail, persist *how* (lesson + episode +
   procedure). Prefer `meedo_observe` / `meedo_ai_advise` / `meedo_consult`.
3. **Recall-first before re-calling APIs** — if Meedo already owns a method
   offline, use it. Live APIs are tutors, not the permanent GM.
4. **Phase, don’t pretend** — do not claim Meedo is expert yet. Do not skip
   embedding because it is not expert yet. Promote ownership only when
   `meedo_study` / offline confidence / judged consultations support it.
5. **Never demote Meedo to “secondary means”** — it is the intended future
   project manager of everything we do. Wire hooks as if succession is the plan.

## Out of scope for this rule

- Inventing brand colors or breaking Shipping SO/Contact locks “for Meedo.”
- Replacing scored engine paths without measure + review.
- World-knowledge training; stay project-specific.
